---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../components/StatusBadge.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Company"
  description="Qinghe Yinghui Filter — automotive filters manufacturer and OEM supplier in the Qinghe filter industry cluster, with entity disclosure, qualification framework and process."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Company', href: '/company/' }]}
>
  <main class="wrap" style="padding-top:2rem;max-width:780px;">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Company</nav>
    <h1>{site.brand} — filter manufacturer and exporter</h1>

    <figure style="margin:1.5rem 0 0;">
      <img
        src="/images/ai/company-facility.webp"
        alt="Modern industrial facility with glass and steel architecture"
        width="1600"
        height="900"
        loading="lazy"
        style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:var(--radius-lg);border:1px solid var(--line);display:block;"
      />
    </figure>

    <section>
      <h2>Brand, entity and domain</h2>
      <p class="notice">
        {site.brand} is the brand presented on {site.domain}. The operating legal entity behind the
        brand is {site.entity.legalName} ({site.entity.legalNameZh}), with unified social credit code{' '}
        {site.entity.creditCode}, registered at {site.entity.address}.
      </p>
      <p class="muted small" style="margin-top:0.75rem;">
        Brand, legal-entity and domain details are provisional pending business-licence verification.
        No certification, customer reference or factory figure is presented without a traceable source.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Positioning</h2>
      <p>{site.positioning}</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Qinghe filter industry cluster</h2>
      <p>
        Qinghe County (Xingtai, Hebei province) is one of China's filter and automotive-component
        industry clusters, home to a concentration of filter and related parts manufacturers. That
        regional position gives buyers access to a dense supply chain across filter media, pleating,
        frame forming and assembly. The cluster is background to this brand's positioning; it does not
        by itself attest to this entity's own qualifications or scale, which are disclosed separately
        as they are verified.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we make</h2>
      <p>
        Thirteen product categories across engine filtration, HVAC and cleanroom air filtration, and
        liquid/metal cartridges, structured around a single efficiency-grade framework. See the{' '}
        <a href="/products/">product centre</a> for the full taxonomy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Qualifications framework</h2>
      <p>
        A filter supplier's qualifications fall into a few auditable categories: management-system
        certification (for example ISO 9001 quality, ISO 14001 environmental, ISO 45001 occupational
        safety), product-level certification against the relevant efficiency standards, and
        factory-level test capability. This entity does not present any certification as held until it
        can be traced to a certificate number. A certification appearing in a third-party catalogue is
        treated as claimed rather than accredited, and is not attributed to this brand.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Manufacturing scale and equipment (industry reference)</h2>
      <p>
        Filter plants in this cluster commonly operate several line types: filter-media production
        (needle-punched and synthetic fibre), pleating (separator and mini-pleat for HEPA), frame
        forming (galvanised and stainless steel), and a quality-test bench for efficiency, leakage and
        pressure drop. These line descriptions are industry-reference framing, not this entity's
        verified equipment list. Factory area, staffing and capacity are marked provisional until
        independently verified.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>
        A typical engagement runs: inquiry with an OE number or drawing, specification confirmation,
        sampling and first-article approval, serial production with pre-shipment inspection, and batch
        documentation. The first article — not the catalogue cross-reference — is what locks fitment,
        and the process is documented so each step is traceable.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Quality and data discipline</h2>
      <p>Every specification field on this site carries a data-status label:</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="data">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Label</th>
              <th scope="col">Meaning</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><StatusBadge status="verified" /></td><td>Value taken directly from a catalogue or standard</td></tr>
            <tr><td><StatusBadge status="catalog-confirmed" /></td><td>Part number or category confirmed from a catalogue</td></tr>
            <tr><td><StatusBadge status="reference" /></td><td>Descriptive application or standard reference</td></tr>
            <tr><td><StatusBadge status="pending" /></td><td>Not published; left blank rather than guessed</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:0.9rem;">
        The{' '}
        <a href={site.dataSubsiteUrl} rel="noopener" target="_blank">data subsite</a>{' '}
        holds the machine-readable record behind each claim.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Certifications and factory facts</h2>
      <p class="notice">
        Certifications, factory area, staffing, production equipment and customer references are
        published on the factory page as they are confirmed. This site publishes no certification
        until it can be traced to a certificate number.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="data">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Channel</th><th scope="col">Value</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Email</strong></td><td><code>{site.entity.email}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Phone / WhatsApp</strong></td><td><code>{site.entity.phone}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Address</strong></td><td><code>{site.entity.address}</code></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="muted small" style="margin-top:0.75rem;">Contact channels are confirmed at the contact page.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
